menu "NearBy One Agent-D bench harness"

    config NEARBY_AGENT_D_RADIO_SMOKE
        bool "Run real Wi-Fi/NimBLE/802.15.4 lifecycle smoke at boot"
        default n
        help
            BENCH_REQUIRED. Sequentially starts/stops the three native radio
            paths inside one complete scan session, drains bounded handoff
            records and reports first-event latency/drop counters. Keep disabled
            in normal firmware so boot never starts discovery automatically.

    config NEARBY_AGENT_D_BOARD_IO_SMOKE
        bool "Probe CST816 and mount SD at boot"
        default n
        help
            BENCH_REQUIRED. Reads raw CST816 samples and mounts FATFS on the
            LCD-shared SPI2 bus. This option never formats the SD card.

    config NEARBY_AGENT_D_LCD_VISUAL_BENCH
        bool "Draw LCD orientation/corner/color test pattern at boot"
        default n
        help
            BENCH_REQUIRED. Draws a deterministic ST7789 pattern for visual
            validation of orientation, 35-pixel gap, inversion and corners.

    config NEARBY_AGENT_D_TOUCH_BENCH
        bool "Log CST816 raw touch range for interactive corner test"
        default n
        help
            BENCH_REQUIRED. Logs raw touch coordinates for 30 seconds so all
            four corners and orientation can be physically checked.

    config NEARBY_AGENT_D_SD_IO_BENCH
        bool "Run non-destructive SD write/read throughput test"
        default n
        help
            BENCH_REQUIRED. Creates, fsyncs, verifies and removes a temporary
            file on the shared-SPI FATFS. Existing card contents are preserved.

    config NEARBY_AGENT_D_SD_DESTRUCTIVE_BENCH
        bool "DESTRUCTIVE: whole-SD format smoke"
        default n
        help
            BENCH_REQUIRED AND DESTRUCTIVE. Erases old partition metadata and
            reformats the entire inserted SD card. Use only a disposable test
            card. This bypasses the product C-preflight flow only to bench the
            board-level D storage primitive itself.

    config NEARBY_AGENT_D_WEB_BENCH
        bool "Run temporary SoftAP/HTTP bench window"
        default n
        help
            BENCH_REQUIRED. Starts the existing Web Management backend, logs
            temporary credentials/address, keeps it available for 120 seconds,
            then stops it and checks gate release.

    config NEARBY_AGENT_D_SPI_CONTENTION_BENCH
        bool "Run simultaneous LCD + SD shared-SPI contention bench"
        default n
        help
            BENCH_REQUIRED. Writes a bounded temporary SD file from a worker
            while the main task repeatedly flushes LCD stripes; reports latency
            and throughput without adding a second SPI transaction lock.

    config NEARBY_AGENT_D_STRESS_BENCH
        bool "Run repeated hardware lifecycle stress"
        default n
        help
            BENCH_REQUIRED. Executes 100 scan/radio and SD mount/unmount cycles
            plus repeated temporary Web Management start/stop cycles. Intended
            only for a supervised physical-board test.

endmenu
